# r1113 Power Grid P6 reruns after pwg8 (rows rewritten 2026-11-13): SQ-PWG-48 to -54 only.
# Runs on the SAME server right after tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113/pwg9.qb (jar backportedPowerGrid-0.6.2-ce-19.2-09,
# level pwg9, group A superflat, spawn-animals=true, ground Y -61, blocks at Y -60). No new boot, no prep of its own:
#   pwg9.qb's prep already copies pwg_probe pwg_grid_probe pwg_p3_probe pwg_p4_probe pwg_p5_probe pwg_p6_probe pwg_p7_probe
#   into OUT/srv/kubejs/server_scripts/zz_<name>.js. Copy the CURRENT tools/scratch_query/pwg_p6_probe.js (fill from NBT,
#   light emission=, assemble lastException) before the boot; if the boot already ran on an older copy: copy it again
#   and `/reload` before this batch (zpwg3 / zpwg4 / zpwg6 / zpwgg are used here).
# Coordinates: X 1085 to 1125, Z 1385 to 1520 (forceloaded in SETUP9P6). pwg9.qb uses X 1095 to 1115, Z 1525 to 1590 and
# leaves doMobSpawning false, doFireTick false (SETUP9); no block overlap (the shared chunk Z 1520 to 1535 holds nothing
# of this batch above Z 1513). The pwg6 / pwg7 boots forceloaded other levels (Z 990 to 1320), not pwg9.
# SETUP9P6 kills the animals generated when the new chunks load (spawn-animals=true), so item and crop reads see none.
# Probe goggle reads log a RuntimeDistCleaner ERROR (client class): no blanket ERROR reject.
# waitlog matches anywhere since the row start; real waits are sleeps (20 ticks = 1 s) plus pace (s after each command).
# Batch deviations from the row text: P6 lines that only wait are built up front so their waits overlap (SQ-PWG-48
# Z 1406 to 1414, SQ-PWG-49 skillet and basin heaters, SQ-PWG-52 LV fixture and factory light).
pace 1

## SQ-PWG-SETUP9P6 | forceload the P6 area X 1085 to 1125, Z 1385 to 1520 (40 chunks); clear the generated animals (not a row)
> forceload add 1085 1385 1125 1520
sleep 6
> gamerule doMobSpawning false
> gamerule doFireTick false
> weather clear
> kill @e[type=!minecraft:player]
sleep 2

## SQ-PWG-48 | PWG-20 heater fan processing (blasting 50 V, smoking 38 V, cold; the fan cools the coil), Dragon Breathing kept, Create fan through a 45 V coil, electric fan + dragon head
shell grep -n -E 'fanProcessingTime|fanPushDistance' pwg9/serverconfig/create-server.toml | head
> zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1400 powergrid:electric_fan facing=east
waitlog \[zpwg3\] done 20
> zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1402 40
> zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1402 0 1100 -60 1400 0
> zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1400 1 1100 -60 1402 1
> zpwg3 place 1102 -60 1400 powergrid:heating_coil facing=north
> zpwg3 src 1102 -60 1403 50
> zpwg3 w 1102 -60 1403 0 1102 -60 1400 0
> zpwg3 w 1102 -60 1400 1 1102 -60 1403 1
# Create fan through a coil (Z 1410), built now so its coil heats during the heater line's wait; motor at 64 RPM first
> zpwg3 place 1098 -60 1410 create:creative_motor facing=east
> zpwg3 scroll 1098 -60 1410 64
> zpwg3 place 1099 -60 1410 create:encased_fan facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1101 -60 1410 powergrid:heating_coil facing=north
> zpwg3 src 1101 -60 1413 45
> zpwg3 w 1101 -60 1413 0 1101 -60 1410 0
> zpwg3 w 1101 -60 1410 1 1101 -60 1413 1
# dragon line (Z 1406) and electric fan with a dragon head (Z 1414)
> zpwg3 place 1098 -60 1406 create:creative_motor facing=east
> zpwg3 scroll 1098 -60 1406 64
> zpwg3 place 1099 -60 1406 create:encased_fan facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1406 minecraft:dragon_wall_head facing=east
> zpwg3 place 1100 -60 1414 powergrid:electric_fan facing=east
> zpwg3 src 1100 -60 1416 40
> zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1416 0 1100 -60 1414 0
> zpwg3 w 1100 -60 1414 1 1100 -60 1416 1
> zpwg3 place 1101 -60 1414 minecraft:dragon_wall_head facing=east
sleep 30
> zpwg6 heater 1102 -60 1400
> zpwg6 fan 1100 -60 1400
> zpwg6 fantype 1102 -60 1400
> zpwg3 drop 1104 -60 1400 minecraft:raw_iron 1
pace 0
repeat 6
> zpwg6 items 1108 -60 1400 12
sleep 0.25
end
repeat 6
> zpwg6 items 1108 -60 1400 12
sleep 2
end
pace 1
> zpwg6 fan 1099 -60 1410
> zpwg6 heater 1101 -60 1410
> zpwg6 fan 1099 -60 1406
> zpwg6 fantype 1100 -60 1406
> zpwg3 drop 1103 -60 1406 minecraft:apple 1
pace 0
repeat 7
> zpwg6 items 1106 -60 1406 12
sleep 2
end
pace 1
> zpwg6 fan 1100 -60 1414
# smoking
> zpwg3 src 1102 -60 1403 38
sleep 30
> zpwg6 heater 1102 -60 1400
> zpwg6 fan 1100 -60 1400
> zpwg3 drop 1104 -60 1400 minecraft:beef 1
pace 0
repeat 6
> zpwg6 items 1108 -60 1400 12
sleep 0.25
end
repeat 6
> zpwg6 items 1108 -60 1400 12
sleep 2
end
pace 1
# cold
> zpwg3 src 1102 -60 1403 0
sleep 30
> zpwg6 heater 1102 -60 1400
> zpwg6 fan 1100 -60 1400
count \[zpwg6\] heater coil state=BLASTING >= 2
expect \[zpwg6\] heater coil state=SMOKING
expect \[zpwg6\] heater coil state=COLD
expect \[zpwg6\] fan powergrid:electric_fan speed=(127\.\d+|128\b)
expect \[zpwg6\] fan create:encased_fan speed=64\b
expect \[zpwg6\] fan stream .*powergrid:heater_blasting
expect \[zpwg6\] fan stream .*powergrid:heater_smoking
expect \[zpwg6\] fantype powergrid:heater_blasting
expect \[zpwg6\] item minecraft:iron_ingot
expect \[zpwg6\] item minecraft:cooked_beef
expect \[zpwg6\] fan stream .*creativeengineering:dragon_breathing
expect \[zpwg6\] fantype creativeengineering:dragon_breathing
expect \[zpwg6\] item minecraft:chorus_fruit
reject processing=powergrid:heater_\w+ time=(11[4-9]|1[2-9]\d|[2-9]\d\d|\d{4,})
reject thermal T=\S+ overheated=true
reject \[zpwg\w*\] error
reject ^(?!.*RuntimeDistCleaner).*(Exception|/ERROR\]).*(powergrid|patryk)
look fan cooling (upstream-same): the coil cools by 1 + 0.01 x RPM (2.28 at 128 RPM, 1.64 at 64 RPM); heater line T about 460 at 50 V (100 W), about 270 at 38 V (58 W); Z 1410 coil at 45 V about 510 (BLASTING, stream heater_blasting after it); flow=east (if west: rerun with -40 V); first processing time read at most 113, products seen in the radius-12 reads (record ticks to iron ingot / cooked beef / chorus fruit; item reads also show the other lines' items); cold: stream none after the coil; electric fan with a dragon head (Z 1414): record the stream (none expected); shell: fanProcessingTime (default 150)

